Two faults in one file: a stray directive in a function body (early) and a
duplicate directive on a later declaration. The declaration scan produces its
fault before the stray sweep runs, but discover reports the source-earliest of
the two (the stray), not whichever phase ran first.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrMisplacedDirective
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app

type T struct{}

func f() {
	//plumb:build
	x := 0
	_ = x
}

//plumb:build
//plumb:build
func NewT() *T { return &T{} }
